invalidImports.js:2:52 lint/nursery/noUnnecessaryStringTrim  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i This trim() call removes whitespace from both ends of the string, but startsWith() only needs it removed from the start.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ import { z as a } from "other-package"; a.string().trim().startsWith("-");
      │                                                    ^^^^^^
    3 │ import * as b from "other-package"; b.string().trim().startsWith("-");
    4 │ import { string as c } from "zod"; c.string().trim().startsWith("-");
  
  i Whitespace at the end of the string can't change the result of startsWith() here.
  
  i Use trimStart() to remove whitespace from the start only.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use trimStart() instead.
  
    1 1 │   /* should generate diagnostics */
